      "note": "Microsoft 365. Exchange Online marks its out-of-office Auto-Submitted: auto-generated with X-Auto-Response-Suppress: All, and no X-Autoreply, so classifyReceived claims it automated, not auto_reply. Automated mail counts as writing back (00181): such a chain is stopped, with a step for the day they are back, rather than paused (G5, G8), the safe direction. PROVENANCE: these headers are modeled on Exchange Online's documented automatic reply (Microsoft's out-of-office troubleshooting page names Auto-Submitted: auto-generated, X-Auto-Response-Suppress: All and X-MS-Exchange-Inbox-Rules-Loop), with example.com addresses; they were not captured from a live mailbox. Read as automated, it stops the chain with a step for the day they are back and never sends more. Whether a Microsoft 365 out-of-office should pause the chain instead (N1) is PR 4's question: a capture is owed before PR 4 merges, and this fixture is replaced by it."
